// ARC-DEL-5 — a failure is rethrown so the infrastructure can retry and
// dead-letter it.
//
// A catch that returns tells the broker the message was handled. The retry
// never fires, the dead-letter queue stays empty, and the work simply did not
// happen — with nothing anywhere saying so. It is the quietest way to lose a
// payment.
//
// Written as the whole `try/catch`: Grit does not bind a bare `catch` clause
// as a pattern here. Verified against fixtures/{fail,pass}/no-swallow-in-handler.ts.
`try { $body } catch { return $value }` where {
  register_diagnostic(
    span = $value,
    message = "ARC-DEL-5: rethrow — returning from a catch acknowledges the message as handled, so the retry never fires."
  )
}
